  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening Women and Youth Engagement in the Electoral and Political Processes in Mongolia (SWYEEPPM)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Mongolia):  .The SWYEEPM activity aims to promote effective, and inclusive citizen participation by youth and women into political and electoral processes. Interventions will foster citizen engagement, constituent-responsive governance, and political accountability through a series of interactive activities, including: (1) workshops on civic engagement (focusing on non-partisan deliberation on political priorities and barriers to inclusivity and accountability); (2) conferences to engage citizens and raise awareness of key policy issues affecting youth and women; (3) comprehensive voter education campaigns, and (4) training workshops for journalists and civil society activists. ..By enabling youth and women to become more informed and active in Mongolia&apos;s democracy, USAID&apos;s SWYEEPPM activity is helping to build a more effective, responsive government, as well as one that will continue to support U.S. aims of promoting democracy, good governance, rule of law, free trade and human rights in the Indo-Pacific and around the world... .</narrative>
  </description>
